course: dictionary
lesson: 12795
title: Elasticity: stretch and spring back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Elasticity is the ability of a material to stretch or bend and then go back to its original shape. It comes from the word «elastic», which means stretchy. When you pull a rubber band and let go, it springs back into shape because it has elasticity.
explain: «The rubber band showed good elasticity when we stretched it.» Here the clues are stretched and the band went back. So elasticity must mean the springy ability to stretch and return. Check by swapping in your meaning: the band could stretch and then return to its shape, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Elasticity has a second meaning, used with money and shopping. It describes how much the amount people buy changes when the price changes. «When the price of ice cream fell, people bought far more of it.» The clue is the change in buying when the price changed.
fact: Elasticity means being able to stretch or bend and then return to the original shape.
fact: «Elastic limit» is the point where a material is stretched too far and does not fully spring back.
fact: «Lose its elasticity» means a material no longer springs back well, like an old, dried-out rubber band.
fact: In science lessons, rubber bands, springs and balloons are used to test elasticity.
fact: In economics, elasticity describes how people react when prices change.
exercise: «The rubber band showed good elasticity when we stretched it.» What does elasticity mean here? | *The ability to stretch and then go back to its shape | A loud snapping noise | The weight of the band | The colour of the band
exercise: «The old rubber band had lost its elasticity and snapped.» What does this tell you? | It is too heavy to stretch | It has grown longer forever | *It no longer springs back well | It is brighter than before
exercise: Which of these shows elasticity when you press it and let go? | A wooden table that never bends | *A spring that bounces back | A stone statue | A brick
test: Which best describes elasticity in money? | *How much the amount people buy changes when the price changes | A shop's total money in the till | The number of coins in a purse | The price of a bag of crisps
test: «Skin and muscles have elasticity, which helps them stretch and return.» What is elasticity in this sentence? | Total weight of the body | A sticky feeling | A bright colour that fades | *The ability to stretch and then return to the original shape
exam: A pupil stretches a balloon, lets go, and it returns to its normal size. Which word best describes this? | Gravity | Friction | *Elasticity | Magnetism
